From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 04:38:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msm8996-common: drop a get_prop for a type the legacy policy
 lacks

checkpolicy stops the build on it:

  sepolicy/vendor/flags_health_check.te:100:ERROR 'unknown type
  vendor_persist_camera_prop'

vendor_persist_camera_prop exists only in device/qcom/sepolicy's prebuilt
API snapshots, not in the legacy-um policy this SoC compiles, so nothing can
be labelled with it and granting access to it means nothing. Removing the
line loses no access.

Checked the rest rather than waiting for checkpolicy to report them one
build at a time: it names only the first. Of the 123 property types
flags_health_check.te references this was the only undefined one, and it is
the only one across all three device policy dirs.
---
 sepolicy/vendor/flags_health_check.te | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sepolicy/vendor/flags_health_check.te b/sepolicy/vendor/flags_health_check.te
index dfb1e177..0f66a431 100644
--- a/sepolicy/vendor/flags_health_check.te
+++ b/sepolicy/vendor/flags_health_check.te
@@ -97,7 +97,6 @@ get_prop(flags_health_check, vendor_nfc_nq_prop)
 get_prop(flags_health_check, vendor_opengles_prop)
 get_prop(flags_health_check, vendor_pd_locater_dbg_prop)
 get_prop(flags_health_check, vendor_per_mgr_state_prop)
-get_prop(flags_health_check, vendor_persist_camera_prop)
 get_prop(flags_health_check, vendor_qcom_ims_prop)
 get_prop(flags_health_check, vendor_qdcmss_prop)
 get_prop(flags_health_check, vendor_qdma_prop)
